Based on Article 19(1) of the Constitution of India, all citizens shall have the right to:

* (a) freedom of speech and expression [chunk-d21f8f962357632e557f6731];
* (b) assemble peaceably and without arms [chunk-d21f8f962357632e557f6731];
* (c) form associations or unions or co-operative societies [chunk-d21f8f962357632e557f6731];
* (d) move freely throughout the territory of India [chunk-d21f8f962357632e557f6731];
* (e) reside and settle in any part of the territory of India [chunk-b9871ed7fee6588a145ac1da];
* [(f) * * * * *] *(Note: Sub-clause (f) was omitted)* [chunk-b9871ed7fee6588a145ac1da, chunk-e7ded89feba8e3774bb1a453]; and
* (g) practise any profession, or to carry on any occupation, trade or business [chunk-b9871ed7fee6588a145ac1da].

Under Article 174(2), the Governor may from time to time:
(a) prorogue the House or either House;
(b) dissolve the Legislative Assembly.
